abstract: >-
  Explicit terraces for all 76,224 non-abelian groups of order 256 (56,070
  groups) and 384 (20,154 groups), in 76,325 witness records (101 groups of
  order 384 have two), together with a standalone Python verifier that also
  checks each record describes a genuine group, nine negative controls that
  the verifier must reject, a coverage check, and a GAP script confirming that
  each record's group is the SmallGroup its id names, with the logs of both
  checks run on this release. Orders 256 and 384 were the cases left open by
  Theorem 32(vi) of the dynamic survey "Sequenceable Groups and Related Topics"
  (M. A. Ollis, Electronic Journal of Combinatorics DS10, version 3, 2025),
  which covers every other non-abelian order up to 511; combined with that
  survey, every non-abelian group of order at most 511 is terraced.
